issue_comments.body:
Updated the route for the current FlashInfer `prepare_all_gather_matmul` signature.

FlashInfer added a keyword-only `max_rows` parameter to `prepare_all_gather_matmul` (flashinfer-ai/flashinfer@f2794d589), and the exact signature check in this route rejected the current API at startup. This revision:

- validates `(inp, w, group, *, backend="auto", max_rows=None, verbose=False)`;
- prepares each packed-QKV launcher once per weight with `max_rows` set to the topology's local row count (1024 at TP4, 512 at TP8), keys the bindings by weight and fails closed if a routed batch ever carries a different row count;
- extends the unit test for the new signature and the single binding per weight.

The route still ends with 80 prepared bindings per rank. Unit test run (`test/registered/unit/models/test_llama_flashinfer_agmm.py`): 11 passed in 7.3 s, run on a CPU node with the PR tree on `PYTHONPATH` (torch 2.13.0a0, Python 3.12) and the two edited files in place.
